ou do, tap all creatures your opponents control, then put a stun counter on each of those creatures. (If a permanent with a stun counter would become untapped, remove one from it instead.)\\nIslandcycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for an Island card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', 'When Orchard Strider enters the battlefield, create two Food tokens. (They\'re artifacts with "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: You gain 3 life.")\\nBasic landcycling {1}{G} ({1}{G}, Discard this card: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', 'When Palace Jailer enters the battlefield, you become the monarch.\\nWhen Palace Jailer enters the battlefield, exile target creature an opponent controls until an opponent becomes the monarch.', 'When Prosperous Innkeeper enters the battlefield, create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")\\nWhenever another creature enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.', 'When Reclamation Sage enters the battlefield, you may destroy target artifact or enchantment.', "When Riders of Rohan enters the battlefield, create two 2/2 red Human Knight creature tokens with trample and haste.\\nDash {4}{R}{W} (You may cast this spell for its dash cost. If you do, it gains haste, and it's returned from the battlefield to its owner's hand at the beginning of the next end step.)", 'When Siege-Gang Commander enters the battlefield, create three 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.\\n{1}{R}, Sacrifice a Goblin: Siege-Gang Commander deals 2 damage to any target.', 'When Wood Elves enters the battlefield, search your library for a Forest card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'When you cast this spell, amass Orcs 5, mill five cards, then return a creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nTrample\\nWhenever a commander an opponent controls dies, the Ring tempts you.', "When your commander deals combat damage to a player, if there is no monarch, you become the monarch.\\nAt the beginning of the monarch's end step, that player draws a card.", 'Whenever Beregond of the Guard or another Human enters the battlefield under your control, creatures you control get +1/+1 and gain vigilance until end of turn.', "Whenever Boromir, Gondor's Hope enters the battlefield or attacks, look at the top six cards of your library. You may reveal a Human or artifact card from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.", "Whenever Flamerush Rider attacks, create a token that's a copy of another target attacking creature and that's tapped and attacking. Exile the token at end of combat.\\nDash {2}{R}{R} (You may cast this spell for its dash cost. If you do, it gains haste, and it's returned from the battlefield to its owner's hand at the beginning of the next end step.)", "Whenever River Kelpie or another permanent enters the battlefield from a graveyard, draw a card.\\nWhenever a player casts a spell from a graveyard, draw a card.\\nPersist (When this creature dies, if it had no -1/-1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control with a -1/-1 counter on it.)", 'Whenever Savvy Hunter attacks or blocks, create a Food token. (It\'s an artifact with "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: You gain 3 life.")\\nSacrifice two Foods: Draw a card.', "Whenever a creature attacks you or a planeswalker you control, that creature's controller loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.", 'Whenever a creature you control attacks, it gets +1/+0 until end of turn for each other attacking creature that shares a creature type with it.', 'Whenever a creature you control leaves the battlefield, if it had counters on it, put those counters on The Ozolith.\\nAt the beginning of combat on your turn, if The Ozolith has counters on it, you may move all counters from The Ozolith onto target creature.', "Whenever a legendary creature with mana value 4 or greater enters the battlefield under your control, you become the monarch.\\nAt the beginning of your end step, if you're the monarch, create two 1/1 white Human Soldier creature tokens.", "Whenever a nonartifact permanent enters the battlefield under your control, you may return another permanent you control that shares a permanent type with it to its owner's hand.", "Whenever a nontoken creature an opponent controls dies, exile it.\\n{2}{B}, Put a creature card exiled with Shelob, Dread Weaver into its owner's graveyard: Put two +1/+1 counters on Shelob. Draw a card.\\n{X}{1}{B}: Put target creature card with mana value X exiled with Shelob onto the battlefield tapped under your control.", "Whenever a player attacks you, target attacking creature gets -2/-0 until end of turn.\\nWhenever a player attacks, if they aren't attacking you, that player chooses an attacking creature. It gets +2/+0 until end of turn.", "Whenever an opponent activates an ability of an artifact, creature, or land on the battlefield, if it isn't a mana ability, Harsh Mentor deals 2 damage to that player.", 'Whenever an opponent taps an artifact for mana, gain control of that artifact until the end of your next turn.', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever another creature with power 2 or less enters the battlefield under your control, you may pay {1}. If you do, draw a card.', 'Whenever equipped creature attacks, it deals damage equal to its power to target creature defending player controls.\\nEquip Elf {2}\\nEquip {5}', 'Whenever one or more creatures attack one of your opponents or a planeswalker they control, those creatures gain menace until end of turn.', 'Whenever one or more other Elves enter the battlefield under your control, create a 1/1 green Elf Warrior creature token. This ability triggers only once each turn.\\n{5}{G}{G}: Elves you control get +2/+2 and gain deathtouch until end of turn.', "Whenever players finish voting, each opponent who voted for a choice you voted for creates a Treasure token. You scry X, where X is the number of opponents who voted for a choice you didn't vote for. Draw a card.", 'Whenever players finish voting, you and each opponent who voted for a choice you voted for may scry 2.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', "Whenever you activate an ability, if it isn't a mana ability, you may pay {2}. If you do, copy that ability. You may choose new targets for the copy.", "Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, amass Orcs X, where X is that spell's mana value. (Put X +1/+1 counters on an Army you control. It's also an Orc. If you don't control an Army, create a 0/0 black Orc Army creature token first.)\\nGoblins and Orcs you control have ward {2}.", 'Whenever you cast a spell with mana value 5 or greater, each opponent reveals the top card of their library. If any of those cards shares a card type with that spell, copy that spell, you may choose new targets for the copy, and each opponent draws a card. Otherwise, you draw a card. (A copy of a permanent spell becomes a token.)', "Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell from your hand during an opponent's turn, exile that card with three time counters on it instead of putting it into your graveyard as it resolves. Then if the exiled card doesn't have suspend, it gains suspend. (At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter from that card. When the last is removed, you may play it without paying its mana cost.)", 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Guttersnipe deals 2 damage to each opponent.', 'Whenever you cast your second spell each turn, draw a card, then create a 0/3 white Wall creature token with defender.\\nAt the beginning of combat on your turn, creatures you control with defender gain exalted until end of turn. (Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each instance of exalted among permanents you control.)', 'Whenever you gain life, put that many ribbon counters on Prize Pig. Then if there are three or more ribbon counters on Prize Pig, remove those counters and untap it.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'Whenever you gain life, target opponent loses that much life.', 'Whenever you gain life, you may pay {2}. If you do, draw a card.\\n{3}{W}: Create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token with lifelink.', 'Whenever you gain life, you may pay {X}, where X is less than or equal to the amount of life you gained. If you do, draw X cards.', 'Will of the council — At the beginning of combat on your turn, if another Elf entered the battlefield under your control this turn, starting with you, each player votes for dominion or guidance. If dominion gets more votes, the Ring tempts you, then you put a +1/+1 counter on your Ring-bearer. If guidance gets more votes or the vote is tied, draw a card.', 'Will of the council — Starting with you, each player votes for return or embark. If return gets more votes, each player returns up to two cards from their graveyard to their hand, then you exile Sail into the West. If embark gets more votes or the vote is tied, each player may discard their hand and draw seven cards.', 'Will of the council — Starting with you, each player votes for time or knowledge. If time gets more votes, take an extra turn after this one. If knowledge gets more votes or the vote is tied, draw three cards.', 'Wind-Scarred Crag enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Wind-Scarred Crag enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}.', 'Woodland Cemetery enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Swamp or a Forest.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}.', 'Woodland Stream enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}.', 'Worn Powerstone enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}.', 'You draw two cards and you lose 2 life.', 'You have no maximum hand size.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', "You may exert Rohirrim Chargers as it attacks. (It won't untap during your next untap step.)\\nWhenever you exert a creature, reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal an Equipment card. Put that card onto the battlefield attached to that creature, then put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.", 'You may play an additional land this turn.\\nDraw a card.', '{1}, Sacrifice Goblin Cratermaker: Choose one —\\n• Goblin Cratermaker deals 2 damage to target creature.\\n• Destroy target colorless nonland permanent.', '{1}, {T}, Discard a card: You gain 4 life.\\n{1}, {T}, Pay 1 life: Create a 0/1 white Goat creature token.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Return target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice an artifact: Draw a card.', "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Wayfarer's Bauble: Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.", '{2}, {T}: Add {B} for each Swamp you control.', "{2}, {T}: Exile another target creature you control. You may return that card to the battlefield under its owner's control. If you don't, at the beginning of the next end step, return that card to the battlefield under its owner's control with a vigilance counter and a lifelink counter on it.", "{2}{U}: Target Goblin, Orc, or Pirate can't be blocked this turn.\\nWhenever Corsairs of Umbar deals combat damage to a player, amass Orcs 3. (Put three +1/+1 counters on an Army you control. It's also an Orc. If you don't control an Army, create a 0/0 black Orc Army creature token first.)", '{G}, {T}: You may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield.', "{R}: All creatures gain trample and haste until end of turn.\\n{1}{G}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\n{2}{W}: Target player gains 5 life.\\n{3}{U}: Target player draws a card.\\n{4}{B}: Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under its owner's control.", '{R}: Inferno Titan gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nWhenever Inferno Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, it deals 3 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three targets.', '{T}, Pay 1 life: Add {G} or {W}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Horizon Canopy: Draw a card.', '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}, Sacrifice Terramorphic Expanse: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.", "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.\\nSacrifice Commander's Sphere: Draw a card.", '{T}: Add one mana of any color that a land an opponent controls could produce.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast a multicolored spell.', '{T}: Add one mana of any type that a land you control could produce.', '{T}: Add two mana in any combination of {U}, {B}, and/or {R}.\\n{3}, {T}: Draw two cards, then discard a card.', '{T}: Add {B}.\\n{T}: Target creature loses first strike or swampwalk until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}. You gain 1 life.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\nBasic landcycling {1} ({1}, Discard this card: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Mind Stone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Untap target land.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}{U}{R}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}{W}, {T}: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt by target attacking creature this turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Field of Ruin: Destroy target nonbasic land an opponent controls. Each player searches their library for a basic land card, puts it onto the battlefield, then shuffles.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}: Target creature with power 3 or less can't be blocked this turn.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}, Sacrifice Throne of the High City: You become the monarch.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}{S}, {T}, Sacrifice Mouth of Ronom: It deals 4 damage to target creature. ({S} can be paid with one mana from a snow source.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{G/U}, {T}: Add {G}{G}, {G}{U}, or {U}{U}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Ghost Quarter: Destroy target land. Its controller may search their library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Wasteland: Destroy target nonbasic land.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}. Sulfurous Springs deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}. Brushland deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}. Battlefield Forge deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}. Talisman of Conviction deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}. Underground River deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}. Talisman of Progress deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Each player gains control of all creatures they own.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Ancient Tomb deals 2 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {G}.', '{T}: Add {R}.\\n{R}, {T}: Target legendary creature gains first strike until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {R}.\\n{T}: Target creature loses all landwalk abilities until end of turn.', "{T}: Add {U}.\\n{1}: Return Oboro, Palace in the Clouds to its owner's hand.", '{T}: Add {U}.\\n{U}, {T}: Untap target legendary permanent.', "{T}: Add {W}.\\n{T}: Return target legendary creature to its owner's hand.", '{T}: Draw two cards. Target opponent gains control of Humble Defector. Activate only during your turn.', '{T}: Untap target Forest.', '{W}, {T}: Search your library for a land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle. Activate only if an opponent controls more lands than you.']
flavor: ['"*Lembas* is more strengthening than any food made by Men."', '"A great smoke rose about us, vapor and steam. Ice fell like rain as I threw down my enemy."\\n—Gandalf', '"A new Power is rising. Against it, the old allies and policies will not avail us at all. There is one choice before us."\\n—Saruman', '"A sword-day, a red day, ere the sun rises! Ride now, ride now! Ride to Gondor!"', '"A time may come soon when there will be need of valor without renown. Yet the deeds will not be less valiant because they are unpraised."\\n—Aragorn', '"About that stream, on this side of the Great River, lies Rohan."\\n—Celeborn', '"Alas for Saruman! The palantir was his downfall, I now perceive. Perilous to us all are the devices of an art deeper than we possess ourselves."\\n—Gandalf', '"All dead, all rotten. Elves and Men and Orcs. There was a great battle here long ago, yes."\\n—Gollum', '"And in the night from Otherworld beyond the Sea there strong and free a storm arose . . ."\\n—*Song of Eärendil*', '"And there are some things, of course, whose side I am altogether *not* on: these *burárum*—these Orcs, and their masters."\\n—Treebeard', '"Are these magic cloaks?" asked Pippin.\\n"I do not know what you mean by that," answered the leader of the Elves.', '"As long as the Shire remains safe, I shall find wandering more bearable; somewhere there is a firm foothold, even if I cannot return."\\n—Frodo', '"Beneath the Moon and under star\\nhe wandered far from northern strands . . .\\nFrom gnashing of the Narrow Ice\\nwhere shadow lies on frozen hills."\\n—*Song of Eärendil*', '"Beregond, if you can, do something to stop any dreadful thing from happening."\\n—Pippin', '"Boom, boom, rumboom, boorar, boom boom, dahrar boom boom, dahrar boom..."', '"Boom, boom, rumboom, boorar, boom boom, dahrar boom boom, dahrar boom…"', '"But I am going to Mordor," said Frodo.\\n"I know that well enough," said Sam. "Of course you are. And I\'m coming with you."', '"But stream and pool is wet and cool: so nice for feet! We only wish to catch a fish, so juicy-sweet!"\\n—Gollum', '"But the Orcs have brought a devilry from Orthanc."\\n—Aragorn', '"But the Ringwraiths themselves cannot be so easily destroyed."\\n—Gandalf', '"Come not between the Nazgûl and his prey! Or he will not slay thee in thy turn. He will bear thee away to the houses of lamentation, where thy flesh shall be devoured, and thy shriveled mind be left naked to the Lidless Eye."', '"Curse the Isengarders! Uglúk u bagronk sha pushdug Saruman-glob búbhosh skai!"', '"Do not be afraid!" said Gandalf. "For you are not going like Frodo to Mordor, but to Minas Tirith, and there you will be as safe as you can be anywhere in these days."', '"Do not let your hearts be troubled. Even now, there is hope left."\\n—Galadriel', '"Do not think that only by singing amid the trees, nor even by the slender arrows of Elven- bows, is this land of Lothlórien maintained and defended against its Enemy."\\n—Galadriel', '"Each year at summer\'s end, I gather water lilies, green leaves and lilies white to please my pretty lady, the last ere the year\'s end to keep them from the winter, to flower by her pretty feet till the snows are melted."', '"Elves are wondrous fair to look upon, or so \'tis said."\\n—Faramir', '"Elves seldom give unguarded advice, for advice is a dangerous gift, even from the wise to the wise."\\n—Gildor', '"Evil things came forth, and they took Minas Ithil and abode in it, and they made it into a place of dread; it is now called Minas Morgul, the Tower of Sorcery."\\n—Elrond', '"Few now have the skill in healing to match such evil weapons."\\n—Strider', '"First name the four, the free peoples:\\nEldest of all, the elf-children . . ."\\n—*Long List of the Ents*', '"First name the four, the free peoples:\\nEldest of all, the elf-children . . ."\\n—Long List of the Ents', '"Go now, Wormtongue, whither you will. But then, if we ever meet again, I shall not be merciful."\\n—Théoden', '"Go! If you trouble us again, you will regret it."\\n—Merry', '"Grudgingly, Lord Denethor permitted me to search among his hoarded scrolls and books."\\n—Gandalf', '"Here, lord, is Herugrim, your ancient blade. It was found in Wormtongue\'s room. Many other things are there which men have missed."\\n—Háma, to Théoden', '"Hope he rekindled, and in hope ended; over death, over dread, over doom lifted out of loss, out of life, unto long glory."\\n—*Eulogy to Théoden*', '"How bright your garden looks!" said Gandalf. "Yes," said Bilbo. "I am very fond indeed of it, and of all the dear old Shire; but I think I need a holiday."', '"How long is it since Saruman bought you? What was the promised price?"', '"Huorns began to move south, as soon as the gates were shut again. Their business was with Orcs I think."\\n—Merry', '"I am getting very suspicious of this Forest and everything in it."\\n—Pippin', '"I daresay there\'s more truth in some of them stories than you reckon."\\n—Sam', '"I do not believe that the world about us will ever again be as it was of old. For the Elves may soon pass to the Sea unhindered and leave Middle-earth forever."\\n—Haldir', '"I go my own way, but your way may go along with mine for a while."', '"I have looked on Moria, and it is very great, but it has become dark and dreadful."\\n—Gimli', '"I have seen three ages in the West of the world, and many defeats, and many fruitless victories."\\n—Elrond', '"I have walked far to find these leaves; for this plant does not grow in the bare hills, but in the thickets away south of the Road."\\n—Strider', '"I hope they haven\'t forgotten how to fight."\\n—Gimli', '"I sang of leaves, of leaves of gold, and leaves of gold there grew:\\nOf wind I sang, a wind there came and in\\nthe branches blew."', '"I stand in the place of the Steward of Gondor, and it is mine to think first of its people. Gondor must be protected."\\n—Prince Imrahil', '"I thank you once more, and I bid you farewell. May your forest grow again in peace."\\n—Aragorn', '"I\'m leaving; for somewhere where I can finish my book, perhaps. I have thought of a nice ending for it: \'And he lived happily ever after to the end of his days.\'"\\n—Bilbo', '"If indeed you look only, as you say, for records of ancient days and the beginnings of the City, read on!"', '"In Dwimordene, in Lórien\\nSeldom have walked the feet of Men,\\nFew mortal eyes have seen the light\\nThat lies there ever, long and bright.\\nGaladriel! Galadriel!"', '"In that golden hall dwells Théoden son of Thengel, King of the Mark of Rohan."\\n—Gandalf', '"In the morning, I shall ride to Edoras to the gathering of the Mark."\\n—Théoden', '"In this place will I abide, and my heirs, unto the ending of the world."', '"Indeed," said Glóin, "if it were not for the Beornings, the passage from Dale to Rivendell would long ago have become impossible. They are valiant Men."', '"Is it not a law in the City that those who wear the black and silver must stay in the Citadel?"\\n—Gandalf', '"Is it not said that no foe has ever taken the Hornburg, if men defended it?"\\n—Aragorn', '"It\'s a dangerous business, Frodo, going out of your door. You step into the Road, and if you don\'t keep your feet, there is no knowing where you might be swept off to."\\n—Bilbo', '"Last night I told you of Sauron, the Dark Lord. The rumors are true: he has arisen again."\\n—Gandalf', '"Learn now the lore of Living Creatures!"', '"Let others a journey new begin,\\nBut I at last with weary feet\\nWill turn towards the lighted inn,\\nMy evening-rest and sleep to meet."\\n—Bilbo\'s song', '"Long have I wandered by roads forgotten, seeking the house of Elrond."', '"Magic rings are, well, magical; and they are rare and curious."\\n—Gandalf', '"My heart rejoices; for you, Estel, shall be among the great whose valor will destroy the Shadow."\\n—Arwen', '"Narsil was broken and its light extinguished, and it has not yet been forged again."\\n—Elrond', '"Never did I see an axe so wielded."\\n—Aragorn', '"No Dwarf could be unmoved by such loveliness."', '"None of the Orcs will ever return out of Lórien."\\n—Haldir', '"Now the great cloud hangs over all the land between here and the Mountains of Shadow; and it is deepening. War has already begun."\\n—Errand-rider of Gondor', '"Now you must be brought before the Lord and the Lady."', '"Precious, precious, precious!"', '"Radagast has much lore of herbs and beasts, and birds are especially his friends."\\n—Gandalf', '"Radagast is, of course, a worthy Wizard, a master of shapes and changes of hue."\\n—Gandalf', '"Regiments of black crows are flying all over. I do not know what they are about, but I think they are spying out the land."\\n—Gandalf', '"Rivendell is a perfect house, whether you like food or sleep or storytelling or singing, or a pleasant mixture of them all."\\n—Bilbo', '"See you soon! I\'ll bring you back an army of Tooks in the morning."\\n—Pippin', '"Seven stars and seven stones and one white tree."\\n—A rhyme of lore', '"Shortcuts make long delays. The country is rough round here, and there are bogs and all kinds of difficulties down in the Marish."\\n—Pippin', '"Sing hey! for the bath at close of day\\nthat washes the weary mud away!\\nA loon is he that will not sing:\\nO! Water Hot is a noble thing!"\\n—*The Bath Song*', '"Smoke rises once more from Mount Doom. The power of the Black Land grows and we are hard beset."\\n—Boromir', '"So it\'s begun at last! I\'ve been itching for trouble all this year."', '"That is the business of Wizards: Wizards are always troubled about the future."\\n—Treebeard', '"That was a mighty show in the dark, my friend!" said Gimli.\\n"But who can say what it hit?" said Legolas.', '"That\'s your tone, is it? Change it, or we\'ll change it for you. You little folk are getting too uppish."', '"The *palantíri* of the Kings of Old: the name meant \'that which looks far away.\' The Orthanc-stone was one, and it is beyond Saruman\'s art."\\n—Gandalf', '"The Dwarves tell no tale; but even as mithril was the foundation of their wealth, so also it was their destruction."\\n—Gandalf', '"The Great Ring shall go now to be an heirloom of the North Kingdom; but records of it shall be left in Gondor, lest a time come when the memory of these great matters shall grow dim."\\n—*Scroll of Isildur*', '"The Mirror of Galadriel shows things that were, and things that are, and things that yet may be."', '"The Realm of Sauron is ended forever!"', '"The Road goes ever on and on,\\nDown from the door where it began.\\nNow far ahead the Road has gone,\\nAnd I must follow, if I can."\\n—Frodo\'s song', '"The Three Rings of the Elves were not made as weapons of war or conquest—that is not their power. Those who made them did not desire strength or domination or hoarded wealth, but understanding, making, and healing, to preserve all things unstained."\\n—Elrond', '"The enemy is at hand! We loosed every arrow that we had, and filled the Dike with Orcs. But it will not halt them long."', '"The houses of the dead are no places for the living."\\n—Gandalf', '"The last Steward of Gondor begs leave to surrender his office."', '"The leaves were long, the grass was green,\\nThe hemlock-umbels tall and fair,\\nAnd in the glade a light was seen\\nOf stars in shadow shimmering."\\n—*Tale of Tinúviel*', '"The oldest rowan-trees were planted by the Ents to try and please the Entwives; but they looked at them and smiled and said that they knew where whiter blossom and richer fruit were growing."\\n—Quickbeam', '"The power of their master is in them, and they stand or fall by him."\\n—Gandalf', '"The strongest must seek a way, say you? But I say: let a plowman plow, but choose an otter for swimming, and choose an Elf for running light over grass and leaf."\\n—Legolas', '"The world is full enough of hurts and mischances without wars to multiply them."', '"The world is indeed full of peril, and in it there are many dark places; in all lands, love is now mingled with grief."\\n—Haldir', '"The Ñoldor, perhaps Fëanor himself, wrought the *palantíri* in days so long ago that the time cannot be measured in years."\\n—Gandalf', '"There are but two courses: to hide the Ring forever; or to unmake it."', '"There are no trees like the trees of that land.\\nFor in the autumn their leaves fall not, but turn to gold."\\n—Legolas', '"There are older and fouler things than Orcs in the deep places of the world."\\n—Gandalf', '"There is food in the wild. You need not be afraid of starving before winter comes."', '"There lie the woods of Lothlórien! That is the fairest of all the dwellings of my people."\\n—Legolas', '"There we sat high up above the floods and watched the drowning of Isengard."\\n—Pippin', '"There\'s some devilry at work in the Shire."\\n—Sam', '"They have no need to ride to war; war already marches on their own lands."\\n—Legolas', '"They tried to pierce your heart with a Morgul-knife which remains in the wound. If they had succeeded, you would have become like they are, only weaker and under their command."\\n—Gandalf', '"This is an Ent house, and there are no seats, I fear. But you may sit on the table. You are thirsty, I expect. Perhaps you are also tired. Drink this!"', '"This is the Window of the Sunset, fairest of all the falls of Ithilien, land of many fountains."\\n—Faramir', '"This is the hour when we draw swords together!"\\n—Aragorn', '"This is worse than Mordor! Much worse, in a way. It comes home to you, as they say, because it is a home, and you remember it before it was all ruined."\\n—Sam', '"Thus is the friendship of the Mark and of Gondor bound with a new bond, and the more do I rejoice."\\n—Éomer', '"To Rivendell, where Elves yet dwell\\nIn glades beneath the misty fell."\\n—Merry and Pippin', '"We have found many of our folk lying slain as they fled thither."\\n—Rider of Rohan', '"We must hasten. The beacons of Gondor are alight. War is kindled."\\n—Gandalf', '"We shall meet bitter cold, if not worse, before we come down on the other side. It will not help us to keep so secret that we are frozen to death."\\n—Boromir', '"Welcome to Caras Galadhon! Here is the city of the Galadhrim where dwell the Lord Celeborn and Galadriel, the Lady of Lórien."\\n—Haldir', '"What aid have you ever brought, Stormcrow? And what aid do you bring now? It was aid from us that you sought the last time you were here."\\n—Wormtongue', '"What roads would any dare to tread if the Dúnedain were all gone into the grave?"\\n—Aragorn', '"When it turns round the black rock, you\'ll see it. Suddenly you\'ll see it above you, and you\'ll want to hide."\\n—Gollum', '"Whereas the light perceives the very heart of the darkness, its own secret has not been discovered."\\n—Haldir', '"Who can now hold the fords when the King of the Nine Riders comes?"\\n—Frodo', '"You are in Rivendell, and you need not worry about anything for the present."\\n—Gandalf', '"You may triumph on the field, for a day. But against the Power that now arises there is no victory."', '"You should see the waterways of Dale, Frodo, and the fountains, and the pools! You should see the terraces and towers upon the Mountain\'s sides!"\\n—Glóin', '"Éowyn Éomund\'s daughter, awake! For your enemy has passed away!"\\n—Aragorn', '"Ónen i-Estel Edain, ú-chebin estel anim."', 'A hundred ladders were raised against the battlements. Over the wall and under the wall the last assault came, sweeping like a dark wave upon a hill of sand.', 'A land defiled, diseased beyond all healing—unless the Great Sea should enter in and wash it with oblivion.', 'A shrill yell went up—they had been seen. There was a ring and clash of steel.', 'All that has been wrought by those who wield the Three will turn to their undoing, and their minds and hearts will become revealed to Sauron, if he regains the One.', 'All that is gold does not glitter,\\nNot all those who wander are lost;\\nThe old that is strong does not wither,\\nDeep roots are not reached by the frost.', 'All through the winter Sam remained as patient as he could. Spring surpassed his wildest hopes.', "Amon Sûl they called it. It was burned and broken, and nothing remains of it now but a tumbled ring, like a rough crown on the old hill's head.", 'Anything that Hobbits had no immediate use for, but were unwilling to throw away, they called a *mathom*. Their dwellings were apt to become rather crowded with mathoms.', 'Aragorn saw the River like a ribbon laid down to Pelargir, and beyond that was a light on the sky that spoke of the Sea. And Gandalf said: "This is your realm, and the heart of the greater realm that shall be."', 'Aragorn took the green stone and held it up, and there came a green fire from his hand.', 'As Frodo put on the Ring and claimed it for his own, the Power in Barad-dûr was shaken, and the Tower trembled from its foundations to its proud and bitter crown.', 'At either end of the Bridge there was a great spiked gate, very gloomy and un-Shirelike.', 'At length they came to Weathertop; and it was then drawing towards evening and the shadow of the hill lay dark on the road.', 'At that moment Gandalf lifted his staff, and crying aloud he smote the bridge before him.', 'Before all went Aragorn with the Flame of the West—Andúril, like a new fire kindled, Narsil reforged as deadly as of old. And upon his brow was the Star of Elendil.', 'Before the shadows of evening were long in happier lands, they went on again with only brief halts until they had come to the very midst of the Dead Marshes.', 'Behold! The power of Mordor was scattering like dust in the wind.', 'Beyond, in the great fief of Belfalas, dwelt Prince Imrahil in his castle of Dol Amroth by the sea.', 'Buckler and corslet, axe and sword,\\nAnd shining spears were laid in hoard.', 'Do not meddle in the affairs of Wizards, for they are subtle and quick to anger.', 'Each cloak was fastened about the neck with a brooch like a green leaf veined with silver.', 'Ent the earthborn, old as mountains.', "Even Sam's vision in the Mirror had not prepared him. The Old Grange on the west side had been knocked down, and its place taken by rows of tarred sheds. All the chestnuts were gone. The banks and hedgerows were broken.", 'Faramir and Éowyn stood forth and set hand in hand; and all there drank to them and were glad.', 'Frodo was hardly less terrified than his companions; he was quaking as if he was bitter cold, but his terror was swallowed up in a sudden temptation to put on the Ring.', 'From afar, Arwen watched over Aragorn, and in hope, she made for him a great and kingly standard.', 'From far away, now dim, now growing, now mounting to the clouds, there came a drumming rumble, a roar, a long echoing roll of ruinous noise.', "Gandalf's fame in the Shire was due mainly to his skill with fires, smokes, and lights.", 'Goldberry came before them, holding a candle. "Have peace now," she said, "until the morning! Heed no nightly noises! For nothing passes door and window here save moonlight and starlight and the wind off the hilltop."', 'Grey ruins falling into darkness, even with sunlight still shining in the sky', 'Grey ruins falling into darkness, even with sunlight still shining in the sky.', 'He hated the Ring and loved it, as he hated and loved himself.', 'His name, of course, was Proudfoot.', 'In a twinkling the table was laid. There was hot soup, cold meats, a blackberry tart, new loaves, slabs of butter, and half a ripe cheese: good plain food, as good as the Shire could show.', 'In the Second Age, Sauron was not yet evil to behold, and the Elven-smiths of Eregion received his aid and grew mighty in craft, whereas he learned all their secrets, and betrayed them, and forged secretly in the Mountain of Fire the One Ring to be their master.', 'In the South, the realm of Gondor long endured, and for a while its splendor grew, its people building high towers and havens for many ships.', 'Isengard began to fill up with black creeping streams and pools. The waters found their way down into shafts and spout holes, until at last Isengard looked like a huge flat saucepan, all steaming and bubbling.', 'It seemed to the tenders of the sick that on the Halfling and on the Lady of Rohan this malady lay heavily. Soon they began to fall down into the darkness, and as the sun turned west, a grey shadow crept over their faces.', 'It was popularly believed, as local legend, that the Hill at Bag End was full of tunnels stuffed with treasure.', 'Legolas built a grey ship in Ithilien, and sailed down Anduin and so over Sea; and with him, it was said, went Gimli the Dwarf.', 'Lórien seemed like a bright ship masted with enchanted trees sailing away from the margin of the grey and leafless world.', 'Merry gazed at the Púkel-men with wonder and pity, as they loomed up mournfully in the dusk.', 'Merry stood at the foot of the green mound, and he wept.', 'Not even an eagle poised against the sun would have marked the hobbits sitting there, under the weight of doom, silent, not moving, shrouded in their thin grey cloaks.', 'Of the seven Rings of Power the Dwarf-kings possessed, three Sauron has recovered, and the others the dragons have consumed.', 'On the growing of vegetables, especially potatoes, Master Hamfast Gamgee was recognized as the leading authority by all in the neighborhood.', 'On the slab runes were deeply graven:\\nBALIN\\nSON OF FUNDIN\\nLORD OF MORIA', 'Once or twice the travelers heard the rush and whine of swan-wings, and looking up they saw a great phalanx streaming along the sky.', 'Out from the beleaguered hills, knights of Gondor, Riders of Rohan, and Dúnedain of the North drove against their wavering foes, piercing the press with the thrust of bitter spears.', 'Over all his works a dark smoke hung and wrapped itself about the sides of Orthanc.', 'Pippin thought he saw groves of trees moving. Could it be that the trees of Fangorn were awake, and the forest was rising, marching over the hills to war?', 'Sam planted the little silver nut in the Party Field where the tree had once been, and he wondered what would come of it.', 'She seemed tall beyond measurement, and beautiful beyond enduring, terrible and worshipful.', 'Soon the rabbits were cut up and lying simmering in their pans with the bunched herbs.', 'Suddenly a song began: a cold murmur, rising and falling, grim, cold, heartless and miserable. The night was railing against the morning of which it was bereaved, and the cold was cursing the warmth for which it hungered.', 'Suddenly as they drew nearer, a terrific baying and barking broke out, and a loud voice was heard shouting: "Grip! Fang! Wolf! Come on, lads!"', 'The Barrow-downs had as sinister a reputation in Hobbit-legend as the Forest itself.', 'The Brandywine flowed slow and broad before them. A large flat ferry-boat was moored beside the landing.', 'The Forest of Drúadan was granted to Ghân-buri-Ghân and his folk, to be their own forever.', 'The Hobbits of the Westfarthing said that one could see the Sea from the top of that tower; but no Hobbit had ever been known to climb it.', 'The Mûmakil of Harad were great beasts, like moving houses, capable of dragging huge towers and engines to war.', 'The Númenóreans had become great mariners, exploring all the seas eastward, and they began to yearn for the West and the forbidden waters, longing for the immortality of the Elves.', 'The Riders were overwhelmed: drowned in the roaring of the river as it carried them away.', 'The Shadow departed, and the Sun was unveiled, and light leaped forth.', 'The Shire had seldom seen so fair a summer, or so rich an autumn; the trees were laden with apples, honey was dripping in the combs, and the corn was tall and full.', 'The Shirrif-house had only one story, narrow windows, and was built of ugly pale bricks, badly laid.', 'The chief city of the Kings of Men was Osgiliath, Citadel of the Stars. Now it is deserted, and in its ruins shadows walk.', 'The dwellings of the Rohirrim lie under the wooded eaves of the White Mountains, hidden in mist and cloud.', 'The earth groaned and quaked. The Towers of the Teeth swayed, tottered, and fell down. The mighty rampart crumbled and the Black Gate was hurled in ruin.', 'The few survivors were rounded up in the woods, and those who surrendered were shown to the borders.', 'The flowers glowed red and golden: snapdragons and sunflowers, and nasturtians trailing all over the turf walls and peeping in at the round windows.', 'The habit of building farmhouses and barns began among the inhabitants of the Marish down by the Brandywine.', 'The hall was long and wide and filled with shadows. Mighty pillars upheld its lofty roof.', 'The high throne was empty. At the foot of its dais, upon the lowest step which was broad and deep, there was a stone chair, black and unadorned, for the Steward of Gondor.', 'The houses and the holes of Shire-Hobbits were often large, and inhabited by large families. Sometimes many generations of relatives lived in comparative peace together in one ancestral and many-tunneled mansion.', 'The keep was called the Hornburg, for a trumpet sounded upon the tower echoed in the Deep behind, as if armies long-forgotten were issuing to war from caves beneath the hills.', 'The light was grey, for the sun had not yet climbed over the black ridges of the Haunted Mountain before them.', 'The noise of bubbling waters came up from the foaming riverbed. Birds were singing, and a wholesome peace lay on the land.', "The one small garden of a free gardener was all Sam's need and due, not a garden swollen to a realm; his own hands to use, not the hands of others to command.", "The pleasant row of old Hobbit-holes in the bank on the north side of the Pool were deserted, and their little gardens that used to run down bright to the water's edge were rank with weeds.", 'The road appeared lonely and forsaken, running down to empty ruins in the mist. But there was an evil feeling in the air.', "The sound of running and falling water was loud, and the evening was filled with a faint scent of trees and flowers, as if summer still lingered in Elrond's gardens.", 'The swift growth of the wild with briar and eglantine and trailing clematis was already drawing a veil over this place.', 'The water of the Morgulduin was silent and steaming, but the twisting vapor that rose from it was deadly cold.', 'The way out lay across a slender bridge of stone. It was an ancient defense of the Dwarves that could only be traversed in single file.', 'The years had gnawed at it, and violent hands had maimed it. Its head was gone, and in its place was set in mockery a round rough-hewn stone, rudely painted in the likeness of a grinning face with one large eye in the midst of its forehead.', 'There are many evil and unfriendly things in the world that have little love for those who go on two legs.', 'There at Pelargir lay the main fleet of Umbar, fifty great ships and smaller vessels beyond count.', 'There loomed against the westward stars a dark black shape: a great barrow stood there.', 'There rose a huge shape of shadow, impenetrable, lightning-crowned, filling all the sky. Enormous it reared above the world, terrible but impotent: for even as it leaned over them, a great wind took it, and it was all blown away.', 'There was a roar and a great confusion of noise. Fires leaped up and licked the roof. The throbbing grew to a great tumult, and the Mountain shook.', 'They began to throw missiles that passed right above the battlement and fell thudding within the first circle of the City.', 'They do not fear the Ringwraiths, for those who have dwelt in the Blessed Realm live at once in both worlds, and against both the Seen and the Unseen they have great power.', 'They looked east to the Shadow and west to the Twilight, and they plighted their troth and were glad.', 'They seemed like black holes in the deep shade behind them. Frodo thought that he heard a faint hiss as of venomous breath and felt a thin piercing chill.', "This was Frodo and Sam's own country, and they found out now that they cared about it more than any other place in the world.", 'Three Rings for the Elven-kings under the sky,\\nSeven for the Dwarf-lords in their halls of stone,\\nNine for Mortal Men doomed to die,\\nOne for the Dark Lord on his dark throne\\nIn the Land of Mordor where the Shadows lie.', 'To his dismay, he could not both fight and keep hold of his treasure.', 'Umbar was a refuge for all the enemies of Gondor—a threat to its coastlands and to all traffic on the sea.', 'Under the boughs of Mirkwood, there was deadly strife of Elves and evil beings.', 'What could not a warrior do in this hour?', "When winter first begins to bite\\nand stones crack in the frosty night,\\nwhen pools are black and trees are bare,\\n'tis evil in the Wild to fare.", 'While the power of Sauron grew, light and living things forsook his borders.']
